<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · song</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bande Utkala Janani</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">written <a href="/years/1912">1912</a>; first sung at Balasore in <a href="/years/1912">1912</a>; state anthem of Odisha from 7 June <a href="/years/2020">2020</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as ବନ୍ଦେ ଉତ୍କଳ ଜନନୀ, Bandē Utkaḷa Jananī</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">&quot;Bande Utkala Janani&quot; (&quot;Glory to the Mother Utkala!&quot;) is a patriotic poem in Odia written by Laxmikanta Mohapatra in 1912. Over the centuries outsiders, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mughal-empire">Mughals</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maratha-empire">Marathas</a> and the British, had ruled <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/odisha">Odisha</a>, and its boundaries had changed with each of them. In the early 20th century a movement for a separate province gathered strength, led by the Utkal Sammilani, a federation of Odias.</p></div>
